screen.COLORED=Colored light
option.COLORED_LIGHTS=Colored ambient light
option.COLORED_LIGHTS.comment=Each lamp lights with its own color (sodium, LED, tritium...). GPU heavy: turn off on weak PCs.
option.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE=Colored light range
option.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE.comment=Size of the region around the player where lamp colors are computed. 64 is lighter.
value.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE.64=64 blocks
value.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE.128=128 blocks
option.LPS_DESATURATION=Sodium removes colors
option.LPS_DESATURATION.comment=Under low-pressure sodium light (a single color, 589 nm) colors disappear. 0 disables.
option.ARC_FLICKER=Electric arc flicker
option.ARC_FLICKER.comment=Electric arc furnace light flickers like welding.
option.CLOUD_LAYERS=Cloud layers
option.CLOUD_LAYERS.comment=Three layers with different patterns give clouds volume. 1 is lighter.
value.CLOUD_LAYERS.1=1 layer
value.CLOUD_LAYERS.3=3 layers
option.CLOUD_LAYER_GAP=Layer spacing
option.CLOUD_RAIN_DROP=Low layer drops in rain
option.CLOUD_RAIN_DROP.comment=In rain the low and middle layers drop; the top layer stays fixed. No rain above it.
option.CLOUD_BIOME_SHIFT=Clouds by biome
option.CLOUD_BIOME_SHIFT.comment=The low layer sits lower in humid biomes and higher in dry ones.
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE=Aerial perspective
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE.comment=Seen from high up, terrain gets a bluish veil that lifts dark contrast, like from an airplane window.
option.AERIAL_STRENGTH=Aerial perspective strength
option.AA_MODE=Anti-aliasing
value.AA_MODE.0=Off
value.AA_MODE.1=FXAA (light)
value.AA_MODE.2=TAA (best)
option.AA_MODE.comment=FXAA is nearly free but slightly blurry and does not stop shimmering. TAA also smooths leaves, fences and thin lines, costing 1-2 ms.
option.TAA_SHARPEN=TAA sharpness
option.TAA_SHARPEN.comment=Restores the sharpness TAA averaging removes. 0 disables.
option.TAA_BLEND=TAA history weight
option.TAA_BLEND.comment=Higher: smoother and steadier, but more ghosting in fast motion.
option.RAIN_STYLE=Rain
value.RAIN_STYLE.0=Minecraft
option.RAIN_STYLE.comment=Realistic: thin streaks lit by the sky, falling faster and fading softly at the edge. Snow: soft, slow flakes.
option.RAIN_OPACITY=Rain visibility
option.RAIN_SPEED=Rain speed
option.SNOW_FOG=Snow fog
option.SNOW_FOG.comment=How much more snow reduces visibility than rain.
value.RAIN_STYLE.1=Realistic (rain and snow)
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Refraction (from above)
option.REFRACTION_STRENGTH=Refraction strength
option.SNELL_WINDOW=Snell's window (underwater)
option.SNELL_WINDOW.comment=Underwater, the outside is only visible within a ~48.6 degree cone; beyond it the surface mirrors the water (total internal reflection).
option.SKY_HAZE=Distance haze
option.SKY_HAZE.comment=How much far objects blend into the sky color behind them. 0 = only at the render edge.
screen.WIND=Wind
option.WAVING_FOLIAGE=Waving foliage
option.WAVING_FOLIAGE.comment=Leaves and plants sway: slow swell + choppy flutter. Stronger and faster in rain and storms. Low cost.
option.WIND_STRENGTH=Wind strength
option.WIND_SPEED=Wind speed
option.FOG_HUMID_STRENGTH=Jungle fog
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Strength of direct sunlight.
option.AMBIENT_STRENGTH.comment=How much skylight brightens shaded areas.
option.AMBIENT_SKY_SCALE.comment=How much the sky color tints shadows (bluish under clear sky, neutral when overcast).
option.GROUND_BOUNCE.comment=Sunlight bounced off the ground, lighting surfaces from below.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of light from torches, lamps and other sources.
option.MIN_LIGHT.comment=Minimum light where there is no light at all, such as caves.
option.EMISSIVE_STRENGTH.comment=Self-glow of light-emitting blocks (bright parts of the texture).
option.TORCH_FLICKER.comment=Torch and fire light flickers slightly.
option.HAND_LIGHT.comment=Holding a light-emitting item lights up around the player.
option.TORCH_R.comment=Red component of the default block light color.
option.TORCH_G.comment=Green component of the default block light color.
option.TORCH_B.comment=Blue component of the default block light color.
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Shadow sharpness. Higher values cost more GPU.
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far shadows are drawn, in blocks.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=How soft shadow edges are.
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Tilts the path of the sun and moon across the sky, in degrees.
option.WIND_STRENGTH.comment=How much leaves and plants sway.
option.WIND_SPEED.comment=How fast leaves and plants sway.
option.WATER_TYPE.comment=How water absorbs light. "Per liquid and biome" uses the right color for fresh, salt and brine water in each biome.
option.BRINE_STYLE.comment=Look of Elementar brine.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_SCALE.comment=How much water darkens and changes color with depth.
option.WATER_WAVE_TYPE.comment=Shape of the surface waves.
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Water reflects what is on screen and the sky. Some cost.
option.SSR_STEPS.comment=Reflection precision. Higher costs more.
option.REFRACTION_STRENGTH.comment=How much waves displace the image of the bottom.
option.WATER_OPACITY.comment=Water opacity for the Classic type.
option.WAVE_STRENGTH.comment=Height of surface waves.
option.WAVE_SPEED.comment=Wave speed.
option.BIOME_SKY.comment=Sky color changes with the biome (vivid, hazy, overcast).
option.PROCEDURAL_CLOUDS.comment=Shader clouds instead of the Minecraft ones.
option.DRY_SKY_VIBRANCE.comment=How deep blue the sky gets in dry biomes.
option.SKY_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Overall sky brightness.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=How much of the sky clouds cover.
option.CLOUD_OPACITY.comment=Cloud opacity.
option.CLOUD_SPEED.comment=How fast clouds move.
option.OVERCAST_STRENGTH.comment=How grey overcast biomes (dark forest, old taigas, swamps) get.
option.FOG_DENSE_STRENGTH.comment=Fog in swamps and mushroom fields.
option.FOG_HUMID_STRENGTH.comment=Humid jungle fog, lighter than dense fog.
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=Height of the lowest cloud layer (Y).
option.CIRRUS_HEIGHT.comment=Height of cirrus, the thin high clouds (Y).
option.ALT_START.comment=Height (Y) where the sky starts changing with altitude.
option.ALT_FULL.comment=Height (Y) where the altitude effect is complete.
option.ALT_SKY_DEEPEN.comment=How dark blue the sky gets up high.
option.ALT_FOG_CLEAR.comment=How much fog clears up high.
option.ALT_SUN_BOOST.comment=How much stronger the sun gets up high.
option.CLOUD_LAYER_GAP.comment=Vertical distance between cloud layers.
option.AERIAL_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the bluish veil over terrain seen from above.
option.CLEAR_ABOVE_CLOUDS.comment=Above the cloud layer there is no rain or overcast.
option.HIGH_ALT_RANGE.comment=How many blocks above the clouds the sky takes to darken.
option.HIGH_ALT_DARKEN.comment=How much the sky darkens far above the clouds.
option.RAIN_OPACITY.comment=How visible rain and snow are.
option.RAIN_SPEED.comment=Fall speed of rain and snow.
option.CHERENKOV_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the blue glow of radioactive blocks and items.
option.CHERENKOV_SPEED.comment=Pulse speed of the Cherenkov glow.
option.CHERENKOV_WATER_BOOST.comment=How much more Cherenkov spreads in or through water.
option.SATURATION.comment=Color saturation of the final image.
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Overall image brightness.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the glow around bright lights.
option.BLOOM_RADIUS.comment=Size of the glow around bright lights.
option.WATER_REFRACTION.comment=The bottom appears displaced by waves, more with depth. Very low cost.
screen.MOBS=Creatures
option.SLIME_TRANSLUCENT=Translucent slimes
option.SLIME_OPACITY=Slime membrane opacity
option.SLIME_TRANSLUCENT.comment=Slimes look like a cell: a translucent membrane with the core, eyes and mouth visible inside. Works with any anti-aliasing.
option.SLIME_OPACITY.comment=How opaque the membrane is where you look at it straight on. The edges are always denser.
